IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccsa-services`
IMPORT `ccsa-qa`

-- Child Care Services Act 2007 (WA) -- cases for the Q&A layer (ccsa-qa.l4): every exported question, for every role
-- and every situation.
--
-- Each question is asked for the role it is not about (where there is one), with every other input an ASSUMEd value
-- that has none: the answer must be `does not arise for you`, and reading any of those inputs would stop the evaluation
-- with an error ("it is an assumed term"). Each question that takes the situation input is asked, for each of its
-- roles, with the situation FALSE: the answer must be `does not arise for you`. The one situation input is a BOOLEAN,
-- so no helper reads a situation enumeration through OTHERWISE (graffiti finding 31); the one new helper that reads an
-- enumeration (`the provider's side of`, over the baseline's `Fee refund`) lists every value.
--
-- For the baseline's seat (the parent) each question is asked on the baseline's own facts, with the answer the
-- baseline's case file asserts, worked by hand from the text, and checked equal to the baseline export's answer on the
-- same facts. The provider's answers are worked by hand from ss 4, 9, 18, 25, 29, 36 and 45A.
--
-- Facts from the WA lives: c066 (10 February 2031), Oliver in long day care three days a week. The creches are the
-- baseline's illustrations (the regulations that prescribe types of service are not deposited).
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Cases -- the Q&A layer`

ASSUME `an unasked fact` IS A BOOLEAN
ASSUME `an unasked service` IS A Service

`as the parent` MEANS `I am the parent of a child who attends the service, or may`
`as the provider` MEANS `I provide the service, or plan to`

§§ `Fixtures (the baseline's)`

`Oliver's long day care, three days a week (c066)` MEANS Service WITH
    `it provides education and care on a regular basis` IS TRUE
    `the children are under 13` IS TRUE
    `who gives the care` IS `a business, organisation or public body`
    `the exclusion` IS `none of the exclusions`
    `the regulations prescribe it as a type this Act applies to` IS FALSE
    `it is run by an approved provider where an approved education and care service is run` IS FALSE

`an outside school hours care service` MEANS Service WITH
    `it provides education and care on a regular basis` IS TRUE
    `the children are under 13` IS TRUE
    `who gives the care` IS `a business, organisation or public body`
    `the exclusion` IS `none of the exclusions`
    `the regulations prescribe it as a type this Act applies to` IS FALSE
    `it is run by an approved provider where an approved education and care service is run` IS FALSE

`Oliver's grandmother minding him herself` MEANS Service WITH
    `it provides education and care on a regular basis` IS TRUE
    `the children are under 13` IS TRUE
    `who gives the care` IS `a family member or guardian, personally`
    `the exclusion` IS `none of the exclusions`
    `the regulations prescribe it as a type this Act applies to` IS FALSE
    `it is run by an approved provider where an approved education and care service is run` IS FALSE

`a family friend minding him, unadvertised` MEANS Service WITH
    `it provides education and care on a regular basis` IS TRUE
    `the children are under 13` IS TRUE
    `who gives the care` IS `a family friend, personally, informally, with no advertised offer`
    `the exclusion` IS `none of the exclusions`
    `the regulations prescribe it as a type this Act applies to` IS FALSE
    `it is run by an approved provider where an approved education and care service is run` IS FALSE

`a family friend who advertised the offer` MEANS Service WITH
    `it provides education and care on a regular basis` IS TRUE
    `the children are under 13` IS TRUE
    `who gives the care` IS `a family friend who advertised the offer`
    `the exclusion` IS `none of the exclusions`
    `the regulations prescribe it as a type this Act applies to` IS FALSE
    `it is run by an approved provider where an approved education and care service is run` IS FALSE

`a swimming school` MEANS Service WITH
    `it provides education and care on a regular basis` IS TRUE
    `the children are under 13` IS TRUE
    `who gives the care` IS `a business, organisation or public body`
    `the exclusion` IS `instruction in a particular activity`
    `the regulations prescribe it as a type this Act applies to` IS FALSE
    `it is run by an approved provider where an approved education and care service is run` IS FALSE

`a creche the National Law excludes and the regulations prescribe (illustrative)` MEANS Service WITH
    `it provides education and care on a regular basis` IS TRUE
    `the children are under 13` IS TRUE
    `who gives the care` IS `a business, organisation or public body`
    `the exclusion` IS `a prescribed disability service or other prescribed class`
    `the regulations prescribe it as a type this Act applies to` IS TRUE
    `it is run by an approved provider where an approved education and care service is run` IS FALSE

`a creche beside an approved centre, run by its approved provider (illustrative)` MEANS Service WITH
    `it provides education and care on a regular basis` IS TRUE
    `the children are under 13` IS TRUE
    `who gives the care` IS `a business, organisation or public body`
    `the exclusion` IS `a prescribed disability service or other prescribed class`
    `the regulations prescribe it as a type this Act applies to` IS TRUE
    `it is run by an approved provider where an approved education and care service is run` IS TRUE

`a centre prescribed under this Act but not excluded from the National Law` MEANS Service WITH
    `it provides education and care on a regular basis` IS TRUE
    `the children are under 13` IS TRUE
    `who gives the care` IS `a business, organisation or public body`
    `the exclusion` IS `none of the exclusions`
    `the regulations prescribe it as a type this Act applies to` IS TRUE
    `it is run by an approved provider where an approved education and care service is run` IS FALSE


`the creche` MEANS `a creche the National Law excludes and the regulations prescribe (illustrative)`
`the associated creche` MEANS `a creche beside an approved centre, run by its approved provider (illustrative)`
`Oliver's centre` MEANS `Oliver's long day care, three days a week (c066)`

§§ `For the parent, and for the provider`

-- s 4: Oliver's long day care is not a child care service under this Act (the National Law governs it); the creche the
-- National Law excludes and the regulations prescribe is.
#ASSERT `Is this service a child care service under the Act` `as the parent` `Oliver's centre` EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Is this service a child care service under the Act` `as the provider` `the creche` EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Is this service a child care service under the Act` `as the parent` `the creche` EQUALS `yes if` (`Is it a child care service under this Act` `the creche`)

-- ss 4, 5B: c066 the National Law; the grandmother, neither law; the creche, this Act; the associated creche, this Act
-- so far as the National Law does not apply.
#ASSERT `Which law governs this service` `as the parent` `Oliver's centre` EQUALS `governed by` `the Education and Care Services National Law (WA)`
#ASSERT `Which law governs this service` `as the parent` `Oliver's grandmother minding him herself` EQUALS `governed by` `neither this Act nor the National Law`
#ASSERT `Which law governs this service` `as the provider` `the creche` EQUALS `governed by` `this Act, as a child care service`
#ASSERT `Which law governs this service` `as the provider` `the associated creche` EQUALS `governed by` `this Act, as an associated children's service, so far as the National Law does not apply`
#ASSERT `Which law governs this service` `as the parent` `a family friend who advertised the offer` EQUALS `governed by` (`Which law governs the service my child attends` `a family friend who advertised the offer`)

-- s 9: c066 needs no licence under this Act (the National Law's approvals instead); the creche needs one, unless a
-- Ministerial order exempts it; the associated creche runs on its service approval.
#ASSERT `Must this service hold a licence` `as the parent` `Oliver's centre` FALSE EQUALS `the licence needed` `none under this Act: the National Law requires a provider approval and service approval instead (s 103)`
#ASSERT `Must this service hold a licence` `as the provider` `the creche` FALSE EQUALS `the licence needed` `a licence under s 9 for this service at this place`
#ASSERT `Must this service hold a licence` `as the provider` `the creche` TRUE EQUALS `the licence needed` `none: it is exempted from s 9 by a Ministerial order under s 45`
#ASSERT `Must this service hold a licence` `as the provider` `the associated creche` FALSE EQUALS `the licence needed` `its National Law service approval counts as its licence (s 5B(2))`
#ASSERT `Must this service hold a licence` `as the parent` `Oliver's grandmother minding him herself` FALSE EQUALS `the licence needed` (`Must the service hold a licence` `Oliver's grandmother minding him herself` FALSE)

-- Lawfulness: the creche under a licence in effect, run in accordance with it: yes; with a renewal lodged in time and
-- undecided: yes (s 22(3)); suspended: no (s 9); run in breach: no (s 20); exempt and compliant: yes; c066: not for this Act.
#ASSERT `Is this service being provided lawfully` `as the parent` `the creche` `in effect` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `lawful or not` `yes: under a licence that has effect`
#ASSERT `Is this service being provided lawfully` `as the provider` `the creche` `its period has ended, but a renewal was lodged in time and is undecided` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `lawful or not` `yes: under a licence that has effect`
#ASSERT `Is this service being provided lawfully` `as the provider` `the creche` `suspended` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `lawful or not` `no: provided without a licence that has effect for it here (s 9 offence)`
#ASSERT `Is this service being provided lawfully` `as the provider` `the creche` `in effect` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `lawful or not` `no: provided in breach of the licence (s 9; s 20 offence)`
#ASSERT `Is this service being provided lawfully` `as the provider` `the creche` `no licence held` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `lawful or not` `yes: under a Ministerial exemption`
#ASSERT `Is this service being provided lawfully` `as the parent` `Oliver's centre` `no licence held` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `lawful or not` `not for this Act: the National Law governs it`
#ASSERT `Is this service being provided lawfully` `as the parent` `the creche` `no licence held` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `lawful or not` (`Is the service lawfully provided under this Act` `the creche` `no licence held` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)

-- s 9 penalty: first offence $12 000, one year, $600 a day; subsequent $24 000, two years, $1 200 a day.
#ASSERT `What is the most the provider can be fined for providing it unlicensed` `as the parent` TRUE EQUALS amount 12000
#ASSERT `What is the most the provider can be fined for providing it unlicensed` `as the provider` FALSE EQUALS amount 24000
#ASSERT `What is the most the provider can be fined for providing it unlicensed` `as the parent` FALSE EQUALS amount (`What is the most the provider can be fined for running unlicensed` FALSE)
#ASSERT `What daily penalty does the provider face for each day unlicensed` `as the provider` TRUE EQUALS amount 600
#ASSERT `What daily penalty does the provider face for each day unlicensed` `as the parent` FALSE EQUALS amount 1200
#ASSERT `What daily penalty does the provider face for each day unlicensed` `as the parent` FALSE EQUALS amount (`What is the daily penalty for running unlicensed` FALSE)
#ASSERT `What is the longest the provider can be imprisoned for providing it unlicensed` `as the provider` TRUE EQUALS months 12
#ASSERT `What is the longest the provider can be imprisoned for providing it unlicensed` `as the parent` FALSE EQUALS months 24
#ASSERT `What is the longest the provider can be imprisoned for providing it unlicensed` `as the parent` TRUE EQUALS months (`What is the longest the provider can be imprisoned for running unlicensed` TRUE)

-- s 18: the creche's supervising officer must be there; not where the regulations provide otherwise; not for c066.
#ASSERT `Must the supervising officer be there while the service runs` `as the provider` `the creche` FALSE FALSE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Must the supervising officer be there while the service runs` `as the provider` `the creche` TRUE FALSE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Must the supervising officer be there while the service runs` `as the parent` `Oliver's centre` FALSE FALSE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Must the supervising officer be there while the service runs` `as the parent` `the creche` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes if` (`Must the supervising officer be present` `the creche` FALSE FALSE)

-- s 36: licensed, or exempt: may advertise; neither: may not.
#ASSERT `May the provider advertise the child care service` `as the provider` TRUE FALSE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `May the provider advertise the child care service` `as the provider` FALSE TRUE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `May the provider advertise the child care service` `as the parent` FALSE FALSE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `May the provider advertise the child care service` `as the parent` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes if` (`May the provider advertise the service` FALSE FALSE)

-- s 25: suspended by notice, at most 60 days, and the CEO must go to the Tribunal within 21 days. No suspension: neither
-- arises.
#ASSERT `For how many days at most can the suspension last` `as the parent` TRUE EQUALS days 60
#ASSERT `For how many days at most can the suspension last` `as the provider` TRUE EQUALS days 60
#ASSERT `For how many days at most can the suspension last` `as the parent` TRUE EQUALS days `What is the longest the CEO can suspend the licence in days`
#ASSERT `For how many days at most can the suspension last` `as the parent` FALSE EQUALS `does not arise for you`
#ASSERT `For how many days at most can the suspension last` `as the provider` FALSE EQUALS `does not arise for you`
#ASSERT `Within how many days must the CEO take the suspension to the Tribunal` `as the provider` TRUE EQUALS days 21
#ASSERT `Within how many days must the CEO take the suspension to the Tribunal` `as the parent` TRUE EQUALS days `Within how many days must the CEO go to the Tribunal`
#ASSERT `Within how many days must the CEO take the suspension to the Tribunal` `as the parent` FALSE EQUALS `does not arise for you`
#ASSERT `Within how many days must the CEO take the suspension to the Tribunal` `as the provider` FALSE EQUALS `does not arise for you`

§§ `For the parent`

-- s 29: the creche's licensee contravened the Act: a refund order is possible; no ground: no; c066: not under this Act.
#ASSERT `Could I get my child care fees refunded` `as the parent` `the creche` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `refund` `possible: the Tribunal may order the licensee to refund my fees, if the CEO alleges and the Tribunal is satisfied grounds exist`
#ASSERT `Could I get my child care fees refunded` `as the parent` `the creche` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `refund` `no: no ground for disciplinary action is stated`
#ASSERT `Could I get my child care fees refunded` `as the parent` `Oliver's centre` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `refund` `not under this Act: it does not license the service`
#ASSERT `Could I get my child care fees refunded` `as the parent` `the creche` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `refund` (`Could I be refunded my fees` `the creche` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Could I get my child care fees refunded` `as the provider` `an unasked service` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` EQUALS `does not arise for you`

-- s 45A(3): never a child.
#ASSERT `May the CEO publish information that identifies my child` `as the parent` EQUALS no
#ASSERT `May the CEO publish information that identifies my child` `as the parent` EQUALS `yes if` `May the CEO publish information identifying my child`
#ASSERT `May the CEO publish information that identifies my child` `as the provider` EQUALS `does not arise for you`

§§ `For the provider`

-- s 29 from the provider's seat: a contravention of the Act: a refund order is possible, even after the licence ends
-- (s 29(5)); no ground: no; the associated creche, on an unacceptable-risk ground: possible; c066: not under this Act.
#ASSERT `Could I be ordered to refund fees` `as the provider` `the creche` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `possible: the Tribunal may order you to refund fees to the parents or others who paid them, if the CEO alleges and the Tribunal is satisfied grounds exist, even after you stop being a licensee (s 29(4)(b)(ii), (5))`
#ASSERT `Could I be ordered to refund fees` `as the provider` `the creche` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: no ground for disciplinary action is stated (s 29(2))`
#ASSERT `Could I be ordered to refund fees` `as the provider` `the associated creche` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `possible: the Tribunal may order you to refund fees to the parents or others who paid them, if the CEO alleges and the Tribunal is satisfied grounds exist, even after you stop being a licensee (s 29(4)(b)(ii), (5))`
#ASSERT `Could I be ordered to refund fees` `as the provider` `Oliver's centre` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not under this Act: it does not license the service`
#ASSERT `Could I be ordered to refund fees` `as the parent` `an unasked service` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` EQUALS `does not arise for you`

-- s 36 penalty: $6 000.
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined for advertising without a licence` `as the provider` EQUALS amount 6000
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined for advertising without a licence` `as the parent` EQUALS `does not arise for you`

-- s 45A: the CEO may name the service or the provider, if satisfied it is in the public interest.
#ASSERT `May the CEO publish information that identifies me or my service` `as the provider` TRUE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `May the CEO publish information that identifies me or my service` `as the provider` FALSE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `May the CEO publish information that identifies me or my service` `as the parent` `an unasked fact` EQUALS `does not arise for you`
